# The program's own way through the records: k = 2, always the top, fan 4,096 on a hop and 512 on a search, 8 hops,
# lambda = 0.05 (Semantics: Personality firmware, "One set of decisions").
#
# A firmware is one human being's selection: how the records are navigated and how an answer is reached. It is a
# file, never a record, so it does not contaminate the knowledge; the same records can be pulled under another.
# Every line is one decision. The decisions a line can make:
#
#   k N                        how far below its rating a standing must still hold, in deviations
#   lambda N                   the tax on another hop
#   fan N                      how many claims that hold an entity are read; one that holds more is reached, not crossed
#   hops N                     how many hops a chain may run
#   top always | within N      whether the top of a set is taken every time, or how near a tie has to be before
#                              another strand can be taken (the temperature of that choice)
#   refuse predicate NAME...   kinds of strand refused before they are scored
#   refuse witness NAME...
#   emit N                     how many constituents a turn may emit: the emission budget STEER is given
#   enough N                   a turn is complete when no more than N (0 to 1) of what its obligations owed at the
#                              start, each word as hard as it pulls, is still owed; 0 unless said: all of it answered
#   fact N                     a member of the set curated by a witness of at least this trust is returned as one
#                              fact, the rest of the set held back; without the line, no such branch fires
#   order witness | standing   on a claim with a part left open: the witness's own order before the standing, or not
#   weigh N KIND...            role weights: strands of these kinds pull N as hard (0 to 1; 1 unless said). A weight is
#                              the firmware's reading, never a change to a standing
#   role by KIND               how hard a word pulls is read from what is attested of it under KIND (its part of speech)
#   role N VALUE...            a word of that VALUE pulls N as hard (0 to 1)
#   shape frechet | outliers N | dtw | edr N
#                              which shape of the tree to favor, and how many variable vertices a match may skip
#   rounds N                   coupling rounds a pass spends: layers, each a routed processing and fold round (Forward 20.2)
#   breadth N                  how many of a round's hardest-responding entities the next round couples from
#   nearest N                  how many entities nearest a curve's centroid the GiST nominates for its shape
#   walks N                    a turn's walkers from each position (0: none); every draw is BLAKE3 of the seed and its place
#   walkfan N                  a place holding more strands than this is reached by a walker, not crossed: it goes home
#   steps N                    how many steps each walker takes
#   restart P                  how often a walker goes home instead of stepping (0 to 1)
#   sure N                     how many standard errors separate two counts of the walks; within them, nothing tells them apart
#   lift N                     how much more often than its base rate a word is observed beside a position for that to ground it
#   elect KEY...               the order the evidence is compared in: grounds continuity agree heads cooccur walks shape confidence shared
#   only predicate NAME...     only strands of these relations are read: a head alone, to measure what it gives (an ablation)
#   tie first | draw | ask     what proposals the evidence cannot tell apart get: the first by ID, a draw, or a question
#   seed observation | session the seed is the observation and this firmware's text, or those and the session and turn too
#
# An instruction set takes the steps of one operation of the forward pass: "for OPERATION", then the decisions that
# hold for it, and for a pull the segments a step takes, in order:
#
#   take fact                  the single fact, when the branch above fires
#   take segment               the rest of the branch the prompt is a run of, followed along what was observed
#   take attestations N        the N strongest strands of the prompt itself
#   take constituents N        the N strongest strands of each of its constituents
#   up RELATION...             for translate: the relations from a word up to its concept, followed back down in
#                              another language
#   language HELD SAYS         for translate: the language of what stands below the concept, read from what holds it
#                              under HELD and what that says under SAYS
#   gloss RELATION             for translate: what is shown of a concept
#   take chain N RELATION...   from each of the N words that pull hardest, the relations followed in order, each by its
#                              witness's order then its standing: where the chain ends is the answer. Chains
#                              parted by | are tried in turn until one reaches its end (a form through its lemma)
k 2
lambda 0.05
hops 8
top always
order witness

# How hard a context word pulls, by its part of speech: the role trust fitted on SemCor's held-out documents, each
# divided by the largest (Research: Trust, "Role trust in word sense disambiguation"). These are measured values, not
# drafted ones; a part of speech the fit does not give has no line. They are this firmware's reading, never a change
# to a standing, and another firmware weighs otherwise.
role by UPOS
role 1 NOUN ADJ NUM
role 0.75 PROPN
role 0.5 VERB ADV ADP PART
role 0.25 PRON DET CCONJ PUNCT
role 0.05 SCONJ
role 0 AUX
# No strand is weighed by its relation: with part of speech in place, per-relation weights did not improve held-out
# accuracy (the same measurement), so every kind of strand pulls as its standing says.

for hop
  fan 4096

for search
  fan 512

for translate
  fan 4096
  # a word up to its concept along the claims the wordnets make, as WN-LMF names them: its sense, the sense's
  # synset, the synset's interlingual concept; and back down in another language. A synset's language is its
  # lexicon's; what is shown of a concept is its synset's definition. Another firmware may go up another way.
  up Sense synset ili
  language Synset language
  gloss Definition

for pull
  fan 4096
  # the evidence a turn weighs: walks from every position, how the trajectory so far attends to a proposal, and the
  # election order over it; a tie is what nothing in the evidence tells apart, and this firmware takes the first by ID
  # a text's language, read as translation reads it: what holds a word under the first (its lexicons' entries) and what
  # that says under the second (the lexicon's language); a rendering in the prompt's language is taken first (Forward:
  # REALIZE, text in the query's language)
  language LexicalEntry language
  # layers: coupling rounds, each carrying on the entities that responded hardest in the round before
  rounds 2
  breadth 64
  nearest 512
  walks 64
  walkfan 512
  steps 4
  restart 0.25
  sure 2
  lift 2
  elect grounds continuity agree heads cooccur walks shape confidence shared
  tie first
  seed observation
  # strands of a kind the pull does not navigate (Sequence: Web 15.x): a sentence's tag layers and an example's marked
  # arguments pull back their tags, not what the sentence is about. A default to be ruled on; the firmware is the inventor's.
  refuse predicate BNC PENN GF PT NER WSL Target Other Sent Verb Noun Adj Prep Adv UPOS XPOS DEPREL FEATS MISC LEMMA type n f itype
  take chain 1 Sense Definition | LEMMA Sense Definition
  # how much of what a prompt's words owe a turn leaves open once it has answered: half, so a word that pulls a
  # quarter as hard (a determiner, a pronoun) is not answered for its own sake once the words that carry the prompt
  # are. A default to be ruled on; the firmware is the inventor's.
  enough 0.5
  take segment
  take attestations 3
  take constituents 1
